AUTOEXEC
  At boot, the boot drive's AUTOEXEC file (text, a command a line) is typed
  into slot 1's command line, a line as each prompt comes back, as if you
  had typed it - after Z is made:
      LANG RU
      NET M4
      RUN 4 SLOTD
  Every line goes to slot 1; a program for another slot: RUN n NAME, as
  above. Holding Shift as CyborgOS starts skips it (the vCPC:
  --no-autoexec; the MSX: always runs).
  No file: nothing happens. AUTOEXEC alone runs it again.
